---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ContentPage from "../../components/ContentPage.astro";
import Feature from "../../components/Feature.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Dongfang Tianjie">
    <ContentPage
        title="東方天界 Dongfang Tianjie"
        description="Second son of the Dongfang Family"
        backHref="/"
    >
        <h2>Dongfang Tianjie</h2>
        
        <Feature
            image={import("../../content/albums/chars/dongfang-tianjie-ref.jpg")}
            alt="Dongfang Tianjie ref sheet"
            title="Reference sheet"
        />

        <p>
            Dongfang Tianjie, second son of the late mad general "Divine Lightning" Dongfang Hongjie, younger brother 
            of the now Marquis of Jiangxia, Dongfang Tianlie. 
        </p>
        <p>
            As the younger brother, Tianjie lives a carefree life in and around the Zhang capital of Khanxanae (Tianjing), spending his days at plays, at teahouses, at tournaments, or alone at his estate practising martial arts. Though not of a high cultivation level, amongst his generation he stands out both for martial ability and flashy technique, fighting with red ribbons moving through the air like a mesmerising dance. The Dongfang family's ancestral arts which he practises focus on speed, dexterity, and precision over brute strength.
        </p>
        <p>
            Tianjie is a kind individual, who doesn't treat man or elf or dwarf as anything lesser because of their differences, and mingles happily in the mid-levels of Damak society. He respects martial ability greatly, but does not look down on anyone who cannot best him, and treats everything like a casual game.
        </p>
        <p>
            One of his particular favourite pasttimes is to join martial arts tournaments anonymously under a false name and human form, fight to the final or semi-final, then transform mid-fight on stage at the perfect moment, dazzling the audience with his splendour. For his golden scales, colourful personality, and somewhat effeminate looks--both as dragon and as man--he slowly gained the nickname "Flower of Tianjing", single-handedly doing untold benefits for dragon--non-dragon relations in the Zhang empire. 
        </p>
        <p>
            Of course, another hobby of his--one less widely spread--is that sometimes, especially after a particularly hard-fought fight with a worthy opponent, he would invite the other back to the Dongfang Estate for tea and some "sparring practice"--something that frustrates Dongfang Tianlie to no end, but the Marquis of Jiangxia had better things to do than to control his little brother's frolicking.
        </p>
        

        <h3>The Marquisate of Jiangxia</h3>
        <p>
            The Marquisate of Jiangxia lay on the east coast, centred around the port of Jiangmen and its commandery of Jiangdao, at the mouth of the Xuan river, the most important seaport in all the Great Yin. The Dongfang clan who controlled the revenues and peoples of this region were one of the wealthiest draconic nobility in the empire. 
        </p>
        <p>
            Near the end of the Great Yin, the leader of the Dongfang Family, and Marquis of Jiangxia was Dongfang Hongjie, a formidable martial artist and well respected within the Yin court.
        </p>
        <p>
            When famine struck the Yin, and the court in Longjing was unable to help, Baron Wu of Shang started his rebellion in the northern plain, cutting southwards through the heart of the empire. The dragon houses rallied around the Marquis of Sixia, Zhang Yujing, and entrenched themselves in the west of the continent. With his back to the eastern sea, Dongfang Hongjie could only lead his army on a brutal campaign westwards to join Zhang forces. Many of his clansmen fell, and he was crippled, losing his wings, but he managed to ferry his two sons and one daughter to safety. 
        </p>
        <p>
            Dongfang Hongjie went mad,
        </p>

    </ContentPage>
</BaseLayout>
